## Summary
Prosecutors in Liguria, Italy, allege that COVID-19 case numbers were manipulated. Governor Giovanni Toti is reported to have admitted to slightly increasing case counts to his chief of staff, Matteo Cozzani. The manipulation allegedly aimed to influence perceptions or decisions related to the pandemic.

## Key Points
- Prosecutors accuse Liguria of manipulating COVID-19 case numbers.
- Governor Giovanni Toti allegedly admitted to increasing case counts.
- The admission was made to Chief of Staff Matteo Cozzani.


